n NLM Catalog](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/nlmcatalog?term=%22Int+J+Mol+Sci%22%5BTitle+Abbreviation%5D)\n-   [Add to Search](#)\n\n. 2021 Jan 30;22(3):1411.\n\ndoi: 10.3390/ijms22031411.\n\n# A Closer Look at the Cellular and Molecular Components of the Deep/Muscular Fasciae\n\n[Caterina Fede](/?term=Fede+C&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\") , [Carmelo Pirri](/?term=Pirri+C&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\") , [Chenglei Fan](/?term=Fan+C&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\") , [Lucia Petrelli](/?term=Petrelli+L&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\") , [Diego Guidolin](/?term=Guidolin+D&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\") , [Raffaele De Caro](/?term=De+Caro+R&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\") , [Carla Stecco](/?term=Stecco+C&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\")\n\nAffiliations Expand\n\n### Affiliation\n\n-   1 Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\n\n-   PMID: **33573365**\n-   PMCID: [PMC7866861](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7866861/)\n-   DOI: [10.3390/ijms22031411](https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms22031411)\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nReview\n\n# A Closer Look at the Cellular and Molecular Components of the Deep/Muscular Fasciae\n\nCaterina Fede et al. Int J Mol Sci. 2021.\n\nShow details\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat Abstract PubMed PMID\n\nInt J Mol Sci\n\nActions\n\n-   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Int+J+Mol+Sci%22%5Bjour%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n-   [Search in NLM Catalog](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/nlmcatalog?term=%22Int+J+Mol+Sci%22%5BTitle+Abbreviation%5D)\n-   [Add to Search](#)\n\n. 2021 Jan 30;22(3):1411.\n\ndoi: 10.3390/ijms22031411.\n\n### Authors\n\n[Caterina Fede](/?term=Fede+C&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\") , [Carmelo Pirri](/?term=Pirri+C&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\") , [Chenglei Fan](/?term=Fan+C&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\") , [Lucia Petrelli](/?term=Petrelli+L&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\") , [Diego Guidolin](/?term=Guidolin+D&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\") , [Raffaele De Caro](/?term=De+Caro+R&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\") , [Carla Stecco](/?term=Stecco+C&cauthor_id=33573365)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\")\n\n### Affiliation\n\n-   1 Department of Neurosciences, Institute of Human Anatomy, University of Padova, 35121 Padua, Italy.\n\n-   PMID: **33573365**\n-   PMCID: [PMC7866861](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7866861/)\n-   DOI: [10.3390/ijms22031411](https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms22031411)\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nFull text links Cite\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat AbstractPubMedPMID\n\n## Abstract\n\nThe fascia can be defined as a dynamic highly complex connective tissue network composed of different types of cells embedded in the extracellular matrix and nervous fibers: each component plays a specific role in the fascial system changing and responding to stimuli in different ways. This review intends to discuss the various components of the fascia and their specific roles; this will be carried out in the effort to shed light on the mechanisms by which they affect the entire network and all body systems. A clear understanding of fascial anatomy from a microscopic viewpoint can further elucidate its physiological and pathological characteristics and facilitate the identification of appropriate treatment strategies.\n\n**Keywords:** cells; extracellular matrix; fascia; nerve.\n\n[PubMed Disclaimer](/disclaimer/)\n\n## Conflict of interest statement\n\nThe authors declare no conflict of interest.\n\n## Figures\n\n [![Figure 1](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/83d0/7866861/9a92f3102202/ijms-22-01411-g001.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/83d0/7866861/3f36c61f8ddd/ijms-22-01411-g001.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFigure 1\n\n**\n\nMicroscopic anatomy of the human…\n\n**\n\nFigure 1\n\n**\n\nMicroscopic anatomy of the human deep/muscular fascia. ( **A** ): Human fascia lata…\n\n**Figure 1**\n\nMicroscopic anatomy of the human deep/muscular fascia. (**A**): Human fascia lata of the thigh—Azan Mallory staining Bar 250 µm; (**B**): schematic representation.\n\n [![Figure 2](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/83d0/7866861/4069b25eca2b/ijms-22-01411-g002.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/83d0/7866861/b4bba2fcbfa0/ijms-22-01411-g002.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFigure 2\n\n**\n\n( **A** , **B** ):…\n\n**\n\nFigure 2\n\n**\n\n( **A** , **B** ): Fasciacytes in Human fascia. ( **A** ): Hematoxylin…\n\n**Figure 2**\n\n(**A**,**B**): Fasciacytes in Human fascia. (**A**): Hematoxylin and Eosin staining, Bar 50 μm—the nuclei were counterstained with hematoxylin; the Fasciacytes are highlighted by black arrows. (**B**): Alcian Blue/MgCl2 0.05 M, Bar 25 μm, the Fasciacytes are highlighted by black arrows. The fasciacytes have round nuclei, cytoplasm restricted to the perinuclear region, and smaller and less elongated cellular processes. (**C**,**D**): Human Monolayer Fascial fibroblasts treated with HU-308: Immunostaining with HABP Antibody. Arrows indicate HA positive vesicles. Bar 50 µm.\n\n [![Figure 3](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/83d0/7866861/46c73e12896d/ijms-22-01411-g003.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/83d0/7866861/ef6f6182f972/ijms-22-01411-g003.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFigure 3\n\n**\n\nTelocyte in Human fascia-Semithin sections,…\n\n**\n\nFigure 3\n\n**\n\nTelocyte in Human fascia-Semithin sections, Toluidine blue staining. Bar 25 µm. The telocytes…\n\n**Figure 3**\n\nTelocyte in Human fascia-Semithin sections, Toluidine blue staining. Bar 25 µm. The telocytes are highlighted by black arrows.\n\n [![Figure 4](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/83d0/7866861/a1f4b3c29e44/ijms-22-01411-g004.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/83d0/7866861/194b5f95e379/ijms-22-01411-g004.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFigure 4\n\n**\n\n( **A** ): Nerve fibers…\n\n**\n\nFigure 4\n\n**\n\n( **A** ): Nerve fibers in a mouse’s thoraco-lumbar fascia, semithin sections, Toluidine…\n\n**Figure 4**\n\n(**A**): Nerve fibers in a mouse’s thoraco-lumbar fascia, semithin sections, Toluidine blue staining (Bar 25 µm); (**B**): network innervation (brown staining lines, S100 Antibody) in thoracolumbar fascia layers. Bar 200 µm. TLF: thoracolumbar fascia. Black arrows: nerve fibers.\n\n[See this image and copyright information in PMC](#)\n\n## References\n\n1.  1.  Pirri C., Todros S., F